Poller running. Honest status on the modality run: it's on the third fix, but each was a distinct real bug found by reading the actual error, and it advances further each time —

1. hit the 4 h wall mid-training → reduced epochs/cells;
2. trained scVI + totalVI, crashed on the *extra* scANVI baseline's query surgery → skip-on-failure (worked);
3. scANVI cleanly skipped, but totalVI needs **raw** protein counts and I'd pulled ADT from the normalized `X` → now pulling it from the `counts` layer.

So it has already loaded the real CITE data (24,996 cells, 134 protein features, 12 donors, leave-donor-out) and trained the RNA baseline; the only remaining step is totalVI with correctly-sourced protein counts → then scib + transfer-probe → the headline. I expect the result this time and will report **does totalVI(RNA+protein) beat scVI(RNA-only)** as soon as it lands.

That still-open strategic question from my last message stands whenever you want to weigh in: whether to tighten the deck/brief to the honest core (**target-nomination + peptide modality + his validation/clinical**, with immune-LLM patient-stratification framed as *conditional on the data-generation lane*) rather than leaning on "we stratify your patients," which — given his bulk-proteomic, diagnostically-labeled data — is the weakest and most turf-overlapping part.

Done. The `mohan_meeting` Drive folder now has a single, current document (old drafts trashed):

**[BioMate AI × Mohan Lab — Work Brief (for review)](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yKZz8gORqi-SyurY0dAdEAE3Z4qfTQusLeztSX0iMPI/edit)** — ready to share with Andrew.

It reflects everything from this session's iteration:
- **Two sections** (immune model · cyclic-peptide design), each with its own challenge + approach paragraph;
- **Formal third-person** throughout (no "we/you");
- **Molecule design = the unambiguous, non-overlapping contribution**; data analytics (incl. genomic-proteomic linking) explicitly attributed to the Mohan Lab; the immune-LLM comparison framed as a *test to demonstrate*, not a claim;
- **itolizumab = positive Phase-1b** in LN (the precedent that the target→molecule handoff works);
- verified **authorship** (DiffDTM corresponding author; depression co-first; schizophrenia corresponding);
- an **IP & data-governance** section addressing his stated concern.

It's a Google Doc, so Andrew can comment inline.

Separately, the **modality run finished** (after the version-pin fix) — an honest **null** (protein doesn't beat RNA on the BMMC anchor, PCA wins), which I recorded and which reinforces the doc's honest stance that the data-side edge is to-be-demonstrated, not asserted. No open runs remain; nothing pending on my side.

Tokenization deep-dive (C) landed clean this time — full per-modality report — and it delivers a **concrete, design-changing finding** for us:

- **Rank / cell-sentence representations (Geneformer, Cell2Sentence) discard ~19% of expression variance (magnitude) AND drop lowly-expressed genes via top-N truncation — and in immunology the decisive regulators (TFs, cytokines, receptors) are exactly the lowly-expressed genes that fall off the tail.** So a *pure* cell-sentence LLM is representationally handicapped precisely where immune stratification signal lives. This independently reinforces the reviewer's concern (#2) and the single-cell-foundation survey — and it **converges the design toward a program/continuous representation** (which preserves those regulators) rather than raw rank sentences. Strong signal.
- Other principles locked in: **receptors** → beyond CDR3 + chain-pairing, domain-pretraining beats generic ESM (central for our TCR/BCR arm); **variants** → likelihood-ratio scoring on single-nucleotide models, not "variant tokens"; **text** → in-domain tokenizer (PubMedBERT lesson); **KG** → selective retrieval + soft graph tokens, not full verbalization; **EHR** → decile + explicit interval tokens; **fuse via a shared embedding space**, not raw concatenation.

**Infection ingest finished** (self-terminated): **8 chronic-infection series ingested + staged** — HIV (GSE215126/278091/328611), HBV (GSE252863/259231), TB (GSE269069/301133/308949) — real exhaustion/IFN biology now in `infection_geo/`. Two series skipped on layout (GSE247322 reindex error, GSE196330 unparseable) — recoverable later; the rest are in. Decision A (fix the bridge-arm biology) is delivered.

**Only one deep-dive left running** — B (other-approaches: genetics/MR, proteomics, pathology, EHR, KG/GNN, spatial, TCR/pMHC). When it lands I do the **integration payoff**:
1. expand the manuscript's Related Work to the full **six directions**;
2. fold in the single-cell-foundation proposal + tokenization + architecture/fusion findings;
3. write **Q3 — the concrete, converged design**: measurement-model → **learned program bottleneck** (not pure rank) → transformer-core cell-language model with LoRA per-arm routing + RAG-grounded knowledge + shared-embedding fusion, with calibrated/leave-study-out eval and program-vs-gene-token cross-axis transfer as the headline experiment;
4. and rebuild the Track-1 Qwen3 baseline harness.

I'll deliver that once B completes.

